WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.290
Think you've seen all the best lightsaber
battles in the galaxy far, far away?

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.680
Well, think again.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.259
The glowing, lightly humming blade has been
the staple weapon of the Star Wars franchise

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:12.120
since its inception in the late 1970s.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.740
But somehow, despite all the lightsaber fights
that fans of the films have seen over the

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.970
years, there's one that still hasn't been
shared with the world.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.730
And it's apparently the best one ever.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.910
Nick Gillard, the stunt coordinator for the
Star Wars prequel trilogy, recently revealed

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:28.711
to Entertainment Weekly that he had mapped
out a lightsaber battle so incredible, it

00:00:28.711 --> 00:00:32.570
would have trumped the one between Obi-Wan
Kenobi, Qui-Gon Jinn, and Darth Maul in The

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.570
Phantom Menace.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.510
He explained that the lightsaber fight that
took place on Utapau in Revenge of the Sith,

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.460
during which Obi-Wan battles against General
Grievous and his bodyguards, looked a little

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.539
different in the original version of the film.

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:48.379
Before ridding the galaxy of General Grievous,
Obi-Wan first needs to dispense of his bodyguards.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:52.239
The theatrical cut of Revenge of the Sith
sees the Jedi Master using the Force to pull

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:56.090
a piece of the ceiling down on five of the
six bodyguards Grievous sets on him.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.270
However, the original version of that scene
would have featured an elaborate battle royale.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:04.460
Unfortunately, when it came down to it, the
production was so far behind on filming that

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.060
they couldn't afford the amount of time the
sequence was going to take to shoot.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.370
Lucas had to make a difficult decision.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.180
Given that the lightsaber battle wasn't integral
to the narrative, he decided to drastically

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.470
cut down on the scene's filming time by simplifying
the scene.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:21.980
With Grievous' bodyguards fighting with their
electro-staffs and Obi-Wan wielding his signature

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:26.020
lightsaber, the scene promises at the outset
to be an electrified battle.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.090
The final version does see Obi-Wan brace himself
for a kind of all-or-nothing fight, but it

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.920
falls a bit flat when he disposes of them
so unceremoniously.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.920
One of the bodyguards survives Obi-Wan's trickery,
leaving the Jedi master to quickly behead

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.020
him in what we can only assume is a highly
watered-down version of the original battle.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:45.960
If the sequence played out like Gillard had
intended it to, it would have been infinitely

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.390
cooler.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.380
Despite sounding like the most epic lightsaber
battle of the Star Wars canon thus far, fans

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.800
have never seen it.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.390
Sadly for them, it likely doesn't exist in
a cinematic capacity, given that Gillard seems

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.870
to be implying that the scene never even made
it to the front of the camera.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:05.340
Still, as disappointing as Gillard's revelation
may be, Revenge of the Sith is full of some

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:09.350
awesome lightsaber battles that many of the
other Star Wars films lack.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:12.920
Even if they didn't get a brawl with Obi-Wan,
the bodyguards get some action at the beginning

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.569
of Revenge of the Sith when Anakin and Obi-Wan
infiltrate Grievous' spaceship to rescue Palpatine

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:18.849
from Count Dooku.

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:23.000
They even seem far more impressive than their
later defeat would seem to imply as they manage

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.129
to hold off Anakin and Obi-Wan long enough
for Grievous to make a dramatic exit.

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:31.030
That set piece also featured an impressive
battle between Anakin and the sith lord Count

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.030
Dooku.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.700
Obi-Wan later fights Grievous and finally
gets rid of him, Mace Windu battles against

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.510
Palpatine, and even Yoda has his own action-packed
faceoff against Palpatine in the senate.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:45.200
Plus, fans are treated to a brutally emotional
stand-off between Obi-Wan and Anakin on Mustafar

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.379
after he discovers his former Padawan has
gone to the dark side.

00:02:48.379 --> 00:02:52.090
Though George Lucas may have cut the best
lightsaber fight in all of Star Wars history

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:55.629
from Revenge of the Sith, he definitely didn't
skimp on Jedi action.

00:02:55.629 --> 00:02:59.470
Whether or not the upcoming Star Wars flick
The Rise of Skywalker will provide fans with

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.019
a lightsaber battle to fill the void of the
missing scene from Revenge of the Sith is

00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:04.280
yet to be seen.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.319
Still, based on the high-flying lightsaber
battles of The Last Jedi and The Force Awakens,

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:09.599
we're not worried.

